<title>JAPAN: TIFFE euroyen ends up on short-covering, JGBs rise.</title>
<headline>TIFFE euroyen ends up on short-covering, JGBs rise.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>May 1 settlement    prev settlement</p>
<p> TIFFE Euroyen 3M (Z)     99.00		   98.98</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The key December three-month euroyen futures contract ended higher on Thursday due to short-covering, and a rise in Japanese government bonds.</p>
<p>&quot;Although the rise in JGBs lent some support, I think the main catalyst behind the rise in euroyen futures was dealers' short-covering,&quot; a city bank trader said.</p>
<p>The fact that share gains were pared in the afternoon also lent support, a brokerage house trader said.</p>
</text>
